especially with the energy bending.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.590
And then I'll do my review.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:52.960
Number 1 - Vaatu fused with Unalaq as predicted
forming the Dark Avatar.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.410
They severed Korra's connection with Raava
and then destroyed her, basically erasing

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.050
her "Avatar Hard Drive" and cutting her off
from her past lives.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.150
So I loved Unalaq during this whole sequence.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.280
He basically became this comic book villain.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.610
If you ever saw the 1990s Batman: The Animated
Series, he actually had "Joker-Face".

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:12.289
But anytime Avatar does something that it's
never done before, it's a HUGE DEAL.

00:01:12.289 --> 00:01:14.679
And we've never seen Dark Avatar before on
the series.

00:01:14.679 --> 00:01:18.159
Obviously after the results of the Finale,
we're not going to see another Dark Avatar

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:20.020
for another 10 Thousand Years at least.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:23.520
But anytime they try something new, I give
them a giant HIGH FIVE!

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.399
Just to explain what happened when they fused:
So Unalaq became more of a conduit for Vaatu.

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:32.350
So normally you'd think that Vaatu would just
be able to sever Raava's connection on his

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.350
own.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.159
He wouldn't need to bond with a human to do
that.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:39.689
But what happens, is when a spirit bonds with
a human like Raava and Vaatu did, they gain

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:41.579
access to the spiritual energy.

00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:44.030
Like when Korra was energy bending at the
end of the episode.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:48.200
So it wasn't just about Unalaq becoming more
powerful, Vaatu gained access to new energy

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.200
as well.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.509
That's how they were able to form that Super
Dark Spirit Avatar at the end.

00:01:53.509 --> 00:01:57.450
Number 2 - Korra learns to Energy Bend with
the help of Tenzin and the Tree Of Life.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:01.719
So this paid huge reference to the Avatar
Last Airbender episode from Book 2 Episode

00:02:01.719 --> 00:02:02.719
19 "The Guru",

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:06.060
where Aang learns about his Chakras and learns
to connect with himself spiritually in the

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.330
way that Korra does, so she can energy bend.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:12.200
So when you see her walking around in space
trying to connect with herself, that's that

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:16.110
Cosmic Level of Spirituality that Guru Pathik
was helping Aang with.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.709
If you recall, Energy Bending is called the
"Lost Form of Bending", that's just because

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:23.240
people have forgotten how to connect with
themselves on that Cosmic Level.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:27.790
But the interesting thing is that Korra still
needs Jinora's help to find the good inside

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.110
of Vaatu, to find Raava inside of Vaatu.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:34.260
That basically just implies that Jinora is
the most powerful spiritual person on Korra

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.260
right now.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.610
Or at least the most in tune with her spirituality.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:41.540
Number 3 - Korra defeats Vaatu and Unalaq
or the Dark Avatar.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:44.189
However you want to think of him, killing
Unalaq in the process.

00:02:44.189 --> 00:02:47.870
And basically supressing Vaatu for another
10 Thousand Years.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:53.400
So we will not see a Dark Avatar again because
Unalaq was killed while they were in the Avatar

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.400
State.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.400
He's basically dead, he's not coming back.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.430
The cycle of resurrection will not happen.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:01.230
But over the next 10 Thousand Years, Vaatu
will slowly grow out of Raava.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.079
So whoever is the Avatar in 10 Thousand Years
will basically have to go through all this

00:03:05.079 --> 00:03:06.079
again.

00:03:06.079 --> 00:03:08.209
Especially if Vaatu tries to form another
Dark Avatar.

00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:13.610
Number 4 - Raava is pulled out of Korra and
basically suppressed or destroyed temporarily,

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.900
erasing Korra's Avatar hard drive.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:20.180
So all those past lives, those past Avatars
weren't destroyed in the process.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.890
They're just cut off from Korra now.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:26.159
So they're people talking to spirits all the
time in the world of Avatar, the Last Airbender

00:03:26.159 --> 00:03:27.700
as well as Legend of Korra.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.700
So they're still out there.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:32.200
They're just living in the giant Spiritual
Data Cloud now with Guru Pathik.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:37.239
So Korra just doesn't have direct and constant
access to them like she did when she was Avatar.

00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:40.890
All that means is that she is basically starting
a New Cycle of Avatars.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.120
Just like Wan did when he first bonded with
Raava.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.580
So essentially she's the "First Avatar" of
a new line of Avatars.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.790
And Number 5 - Korra left the Spirit Portals
open, allowing spirits to pass in to the physical

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.630
realm and roam free with humans.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:55.489
So this is going to figure in Books 3 and
4.

00:03:55.489 --> 00:03:57.159
But now, spirits will be roaming everywhere.

00:03:57.159 --> 00:04:01.040
So we will definitely be seeing a lot of old
spirits come back in Book 3 and Book 4.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.310
So if you have any favorite spirits like the
face of Koh, they'll probably come back in

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.310
Book 3 and 4.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:08.370
Book 3 by the way is also an Earth Kingdom
book, they're going to be dealing with a lot

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.099
of Earth Kingdom stories.

00:04:10.099 --> 00:04:13.409
Just like Avatar Last Airbender, so it's all
about cycles.

00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:15.019
But what did I think of the Finale?

00:04:15.019 --> 00:04:19.100
Overall Beginnings is still my favorite episode
of Legend of Korra of all time.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:23.870
But I really liked the way that the Finale
paid off a lot of classic stories like "The

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.900
Guru" as well as answering a lot of our big
questions.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:30.139
And giving us an interesting to go in Books
3 and 4.

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:31.699
Especially with all the spirits flying around
now.

00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:35.520
The only thing I thought they could have done
better, was explain a little bit more about

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:40.350
the technical aspects of what Korra was doing
with her powers in this Final Battle.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:44.419
So, just because Korra became the Avatar,
she was born as the Avatar as a baby, did

00:04:44.419 --> 00:04:48.270
not mean she automatically knew how to use
all of her powers instantly.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:52.660
And basically, in this episode she learns
to Energy Bend within like 2 minutes.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.310
And automatically knows how to use all of
those powers.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.560
So that's my only small complaint, it's not
a big complaint.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.639
But this is only because Avatar Legend of
Korra has half the number of episodes that

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:05.020
Avatar Last Airbender had to tell the same
story.

